# Mariner: down through Mars's thin air. Heat shield first,
# the parachute once slow, then the lander's engine for the
# last of it (Mars's air alone cannot slow a lander enough:
# a parachute leaves it ~50 m/s).
#
# Arrive with the periapsis in the air (or plan "Come down"
# from orbit), then send this well before reaching the air:
# minutes of light away, it has to fly itself.

# Leave the upper stage; the shield faces the air.
stage
sas retrograde
wait until altitude < 125 km
log Entry interface

# Slow enough: the parachute (stage 4).
wait until speed < 400 m/s
stage
log Parachute

# Shield off, engine lit (stage 5); sink at a safe speed.
wait until altitude < 3 km
stage
log Powered descent
descend 15 m/s
wait until altitude < 150 m
descend 2 m/s
wait until landed
throttle off
log Landed
science
transmit
